A BARE RUN MUST NOT TOUCH SHARED STATE, AND NO ALLOWLIST COVERS THIS.
tools/bare_run_writers.py declares paths INSIDE the repo. A write
to the lock registry, to .git/config or to the worktree list
reaches every other clone on this box, and the session that reads
it next has no way to tell it came from a sweep.

THIS IS THE CASE THIS TOOL USED TO MISS ENTIRELY. Before 2026-10-08 it
compared only `git status`, so tools/session_lock_check.py taking a
lock on a bare run was reported CLEAN.
